 },
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "(Push) is an isomorphism for $F/E$ finite",
 "statement": "For finite extensions $E\\le F$ of $\\mathbf Q_\\ell$ inside $\\Qlb$ and every morphism of schemes\n$f\\colon X\\to Y$, the comparison (Push) ([def-sfb-derived-push-hom]) for the coefficient change\n$E\\to F$ ([def-sfb-subfield-coefficient-map]; flat by [lem-sfb-subfield-flat]),\n\n$$\nT^Y_{E,F}\\circ Rf_*\\longrightarrow Rf_*\\circ T^X_{E,F},\n$$\n\nis an isomorphism of functors on the unbounded derived category $D(\\Mod_{E_X})$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/sk-prop-sfb-finite-extension-compatibility/lem-sfb-subfield-push-iso.md",
  "place": "node lem-sfb-subfield-push-iso, order 1754"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sfb-derived-push-hom",
  "def-sfb-subfield-coefficient-map",
  "lem-sfb-subfield-flat"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By the proof of [lem-sfb-subfield-flat], a basis of $F$ over $E$ gives $F_X\\cong E_X^n$ and\n$F_Y\\cong E_Y^n$, compatibly with $\\eta_f$ (both come from the same isomorphism on the point).\nAfter restriction of scalars to $E$, which is conservative, both sides of (Push) become\n$(Rf_*K)^n$ and the comparison becomes the canonical map\n$\\bigoplus^nRf_*K\\to Rf_*\\bigoplus^nK$, an isomorphism since $Rf_*$ is additive.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sfb-subfield-flat"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "lem-sfb-subfield-flat"
 ],
